an incredible compliment, or passed an

87
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:23,940
exam with flying colors?

88
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:27,540
Because for 99 % of human

89
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:30,860
evolution, social belonging was not about politeness.

90
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:33,620
It was the difference between life and death.

91
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:36,620
Our ancestors survived in nomadic bands

92
00:03:36,620 --> 00:03:38,720
of 50 to 150 people.

93
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:40,900
In that harsh world,

94
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:43,880
being rejected, ostracized, or cast out

95
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:45,760
of the tribe was a literal death sentence.

96
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:48,380
A physical wound could heal.

97
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:51,580
But social banishment meant you starved,

98
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:54,080
froze, or were hunted alone in the dark.

99
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:58,620
In 2003, landmark neuroimaging research at

100
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:00,600
UCLA proved something shocking,

101
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:03,340
social exclusion and physical agony light

102
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:04,960
up the exact same neural pain

103
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:06,200
pathways in your brain.

104
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:09,780
Your dorsal anterior singular cortex does

105
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:11,320
not know the difference between a

106
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,200
broken leg and public humiliation.

107
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:16,100
It hurts the same because evolution

108
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:17,100
