115
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:34,100
It stores it under maximum priority, replay this.

116
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:37,460
Memorize this. Never do this again,

117
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:39,380
or we will be abandoned in the cold.

118
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:42,260
Your modern brain is running Stone

119
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:43,560
Age operating software.

120
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:46,980
It cannot comprehend that accidentally waving

121
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:48,280
at a stranger in a coffee

122
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:50,380
shop won't get you banished into the wilderness.

123
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:52,880
But here is the grand cognitive

124
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:55,140
illusion that makes nocturnal cringe so

125
00:04:55,140 --> 00:04:57,260
excruciating, the spotlight effect.

126
00:04:57,980 --> 00:04:59,620
In the year 2000,

127
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:02,500
legendary psychologist Thomas Gilevich and his

128
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:04,060
team at Cornell ran a series

129
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:05,740
of landmark social experiments.

130
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,400
They had participants put on an

131
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,220
intentionally embarrassing t -shirt,

132
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:12,360
featuring a giant face of singer

133
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:14,400
Barry Manolo, and walk into a

134
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:15,760
